  "DivisionNotes": [
    "TemporalNesting is true because the leads-to operator (~>) used in Prop unfolds to [](P => <>Q), which contains a nested diamond inside a box.",
    "All action operators (PASSIVE_OPEN, ACTIVE_OPEN, CLOSE_*, SEND, SynSent, ..., User, System, Reset, Next) are placed in ActionDefNames since they contain primed variables or disjoin/conjoin actions; only structural value definitions (States, vars) appear in OperatorDefNames_ValueDef.",
    "TypeOK and Inv are state-predicate invariants; Spec and Prop are temporal-formula definitions; Init is the initial-state predicate.",
    "Two anonymous UNCHANGED phrases (UNCHANGED network, UNCHANGED tcb) reference single variables, so they are placed in UnchangedExprs_VarRef rather than UnchangedExprs_Explicit (which is reserved for tuple-form UNCHANGED <<...>>)."
  ]
